<Panels>
  <config><![CDATA[{
  "published": true,
  "game_id": 73,
  "created_at": "2026-03-30T18:22:07.000Z",
  "level_num": "custom",
  "user_id": 18605,
  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "panels": [
      {
        "text": "## Vibe Check\nIn the previous level, you explored push/pop and shift/unshift. Let’s take a deeper look at what was happening.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/809b5a7e2cb868b5e9adfd0ef44f837e-push pop.png",
        "key": "pl-aif-2-U3-push-pop-panel-075d2570-c144-404c-a815-d7c99dd7f63a",
        "layout": "text-bottom-right"
      },
      {
        "text": "## Push\nHere,  the Bruno Mars song, \"Talking to the Moon\", is entered in the input box and  push button is clicked. \n\nYou can see the song goes to the end of the queue.\n.\n\nLet’s see what is happening inside the code. ",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/0a67fde4c25138827ec330e834dfea3e-push pop (1).png",
        "key": "pl-aif-2-U3-push-pop-panel-75914d07-11af-4307-a647-9e668d3a7e59",
        "layout": "text-bottom-right"
      },
      {
        "text": "## Input variables \n\nInside a function named `addRequest`, we see lines of code that store the user input in variables for the song and the artist using the element names for the input boxes from the `HTML` file. \n",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/a122eaa9cc3dbef1d0bfcacfe5ef45e9-push pop (2).png",
        "key": "pl-aif-2-U3-push-pop-panel-eb71e0a3-a44d-47de-b617-7ecbb8aa8dec",
        "layout": "text-bottom-right"
      },
      {
        "text": "## Conditional \n\nThe if statement checks to make sure the values are not (!) empty. ",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/05f3825bf7b6956febe32e59d5832ca8-push pop (3).png",
        "key": "pl-aif-2-U3-push-pop-panel-26b0abdd-b976-4a88-913b-9720fea537e7",
        "layout": "text-bottom-right"
      },
      {
        "text": "## Push\n\nIf both inputs have values, `push()` adds the song (s) to the end of the songs array and the artist (a) to the end of the artists array.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/ebf2274b71090eee2137073ca22fbe8a-push pop (4).png",
        "key": "pl-aif-2-U3-push-pop-panel-36008772-71aa-43ec-bdb4-20b8605c1f08",
        "layout": "text-bottom-right"
      },
      {
        "text": "## Render \n\nFinally, `render()` updates the display so the new song appears in the queue.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/9db85b1e2f584fe8bd3cd71ba89ecfc0-push pop (5).png",
        "key": "pl-aif-2-U3-push-pop-panel-ce1eaa18-1cfb-4bf1-9218-02a25523c51e",
        "layout": "text-bottom-right"
      },
      {
        "text": "## Pop \n\nNext, when the pop button is pressed, the last item on the list is removed. \n",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/4b5d309a05a02c6fd45ab1dd36aec5fb-push pop (6).png",
        "key": "pl-aif-2-U3-push-pop-panel-66a95b4b-1816-4cfb-9de5-a582a0a165f7",
        "layout": "text-bottom-right"
      },
      {
        "text": "## Pop\n\nWhen the pop button is pushed the function, called `vetoLast`, is called. \n\n\nIn this function, the `pop()` method is applied to the songs and artist elements in the artist array removing the last item on the list. No input was taking from the user. \n\n\nThe updated array is rendered and displayed in the song queue. ",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/cc7b13492380b9fdb5c0e65be211eaa4-push pop (7).png",
        "key": "pl-aif-2-U3-push-pop-panel-b2e6ee3f-28ac-4cf7-a8e2-80d3ae909a9e",
        "layout": "text-bottom-right"
      },
      {
        "text": "## Shift \n\nWhen the play next or shift button is pressed, the song at the top of the queue is removed and replaced with the next item in the songs array.  ",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/5037653e90be353268994042c3e513aa-push pop (8).png",
        "key": "pl-aif-2-U3-push-pop-panel-bf48370b-9776-4000-b876-264b74363993",
        "layout": "text-bottom-right"
      },
      {
        "text": "## Shift \n\nThe `playNext` function is called when the Play next (shift) button is pressed. This function uses the `shift()` method for the songs and artist in the array causing the first element to be removed and replaced by the second element. ",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/e1dccac6b8ca239c64ec718b2a11c839-push pop (9).png",
        "key": "pl-aif-2-U3-push-pop-panel-44efc6ce-6424-415c-95e4-b6f01624743a",
        "layout": "text-bottom-right"
      },
      {
        "text": "## Unshift\n\nFinally, the unshift, or VIP Bump button, puts the imputed song and artist to the front of the line. ",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/fdb188f0c4910213838058675a835961-push pop (10).png",
        "key": "pl-aif-2-U3-push-pop-panel-0cbf878b-2575-4fd4-b4b5-66b643fdae8c",
        "layout": "text-bottom-right"
      },
      {
        "text": "## Unshift\n\nYou can see the code is similar to the previous push function in that it takes the input, checks to make sure the input is not blank, and then uses the `unshift()` method to put the inputted song at the front of the line. \n\n\nHowever, this is not the intended use of the button. ",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/3941c4fe0f69797b6762487a0b3ad973-push pop (11).png",
        "key": "pl-aif-2-U3-push-pop-panel-fd92300f-1019-4d8a-b584-7dd9fac472c8",
        "layout": "text-bottom-right"
      },
      {
        "text": "## VIP Bump\nThe activity asks you to adjust the code to automatically put your favorite song and artist to the front of the code. This way, whenever you press the VIP Bump, your favorite song goes to the top of the queue. ",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/89dfc7571b02bb027b57b6dab444bdf5-push pop (12).png",
        "key": "pl-aif-2-U3-push-pop-panel-85cdc2ba-334c-4ef5-b948-c0afa5cd9c57",
        "layout": "text-bottom-right"
      },
      {
        "text": "To do this, inside the `vipBump` function, we need to remove the input variables for s (song) and a (artist) along with the the if statement to check if the input is blank. \n\nThat leaves us with using the `unshift()` method on songs and artists by playing a specific song and artist using a String. \n",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/d92f27b9aeef9299507b4e1f35d451d1-push pop (13).png",
        "key": "pl-aif-2-U3-push-pop-panel-f7460683-ef8f-4714-9ca4-ef8bbe8b194d"
      },
      {
        "text": "## To review: \n- **push()**- adds an item to the end of an array\n- **pop ()** - removes the last item of an array\n- **shift()** - removes the first item in the array\n- **unshift()** - adds a new item to the front of an array\n",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/2d8df8c6a70f793eedc93a8706da852b-push pop (14).png",
        "key": "pl-aif-2-U3-push-pop-panel-32e863af-b758-4720-95e6-f8031893ff7d",
        "layout": "text-bottom-right"
      }
    ],
    "name_suffix": "_2024",
    "offer_browser_tts": "false"
  },
  "audit_log": "[{\"changed_at\":\"2026-03-30T18:22:07.680+00:00\",\"changed\":[\"cloned from \\\"pl-aif-2-U2-functions-panel\\\"\"],\"cloned_from\":\"pl-aif-2-U2-functions-panel\"},{\"changed_at\":\"2026-03-31 16:02:21 +0000\",\"changed\":[\"panels\"],\"changed_by_id\":19028,\"changed_by_email\":\"amanda.dennard@code.org\"},{\"changed_at\":\"2026-03-31 16:05:21 +0000\",\"changed\":[\"panels\"],\"changed_by_id\":19028,\"changed_by_email\":\"amanda.dennard@code.org\"},{\"changed_at\":\"2026-03-31 16:07:00 +0000\",\"changed\":[\"panels\"],\"changed_by_id\":19028,\"changed_by_email\":\"amanda.dennard@code.org\"}]"
}]]></config>
